{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "881b0544",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Variables at a fixed period\n",
    "\n",
    "Some relations refer to a variable in **one particular period**, the same period whatever the\n",
    "period being calculated: an index with 2015 = 100, a value in the prices of a base year, a\n",
    "share calibrated to the level of a reference year. ModelFlow writes this as `X(2015)`, the value\n",
    "of `X` in 2015:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "> index = x/x(2015)*100\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Before, the usual workaround was an extra exogenous variable holding the 2015 value in every\n",
    "row. `X(2015)` does the same without the extra column, and it also works when `X` is endogenous.\n",
    "\n",
    "This chapter covers the syntax, what happens in a model, which solvers can be used, and how\n",
    "fixed periods are handled in estimation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "8f4daaee",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from modelclass import model\n",
    "from modelconstruct_estimation import Makemodel\n",
    "from modelestimator_new import Estimate_ols, Estimate_nls_lmfit"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2e6699d7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The syntax\n",
    "\n",
    "A fixed period is written in the parentheses where a lag or a lead goes. The difference is the\n",
    "sign: a lag or a lead **always** has a sign, a fixed period never does.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Written | Meaning |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `X(-1)` | `X` one period before the current period (a lag) |\n",
    "| `X(+1)` | `X` one period after the current period (a lead) |\n",
    "| `X(2015)` | `X` in 2015: an unsigned number with at least 4 digits is a year |\n",
    "| `X('2015Q1')` | `X` in the period with the index label `'2015Q1'` -- a quarterly model |\n",
    "| `X('2015-03')` | `X` in March 2015 -- a monthly model |\n",
    "\n",
    "A period in quotes is the key used to index the DataFrame, exactly as in `df.loc['2015Q1']`.\n",
    "`X('2015')` and `X(2015)` are the same period. A short label, like `X('5')`, needs the quotes.\n",
    "\n",
    "Both forms are legal Python, so equations with fixed periods can also be read by the estimators,\n",
    "see the last section."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8a149bff",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## In a model\n",
    "\n",
    "A small recursive model: `Y` is `X` indexed to 2002, and `Z` adds the 2005 value of `X` to\n",
    "last period's `Y`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "86b3e473",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "years = list(range(2000, 2011))\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame({'X': np.linspace(10, 20, len(years))}, index=years)\n",
    "\n",
    "mfix = model(\"\"\"\n",
    "Y = X/X(2002)*100\n",
    "Z = Y(-1) + X(2005)\n",
    "\"\"\", modelname='fixdemo')\n",
    "\n",
    "res = mfix(df, 2003, 2010)\n",
    "res"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dfcba23b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`Y` is 100 where `X` equals its 2002 value, and `Z` carries the 2005 value of `X` in every\n",
    "period. The model knows which variables it reads at a fixed period, and which periods they are:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5cd6ced7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(f'{mfix.fixed_terms=}')\n",
    "print(f'{mfix.fixed_periods=}')\n",
    "print(f'solved with {mfix.model_solver.__name__}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "58645da0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### How it works\n",
    "\n",
    "Only the **ng solvers** (`xgenr_ng`, `sim_ng`, `newton_ng`, `newtonstack_ng`, ...) can evaluate a\n",
    "fixed period. When a model refers to one, calling the model picks the ng version of the solver it\n",
    "would otherwise have used. The legacy solvers raise an exception.\n",
    "\n",
    "The generated code reads `X(2002)` from the **row of 2002** in the data -- a constant, while a lag\n",
    "is read relative to the row being calculated. Here `values[2,...]` is `X` in 2002, the third row:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "aa5d7c19",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(mfix.make_los_text)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "088ee450",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Because the row number is compiled into the code, the code is generated again when the same\n",
    "columns come with another index -- here the DataFrame starts in 2001 instead of 2000, and the\n",
    "result is the same. The period must be in the DataFrame; if it is not, the solve stops with an\n",
    "error:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ae00a9ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "late = mfix(df.loc[2001:], 2003, 2010)\n",
    "print('same result with another index:', np.allclose(late.loc[2003:, 'Y'], res.loc[2003:, 'Y']))\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    mfix(df.loc[2003:], 2004, 2010)\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f'{type(e).__name__}: {e}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b510dae5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### On a DataFrame with `mfcalc`\n",
    "\n",
    "`mfcalc` runs equations directly on a DataFrame, so a fixed period works there too:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "667b3c0c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df.mfcalc('IDX = X/X(2002)*100')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ad6e64f9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Quarterly and monthly data\n",
    "\n",
    "With a quarterly or monthly index the period is given as text, the label the DataFrame is\n",
    "indexed with:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "87afce92",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "qidx = pd.period_range('2001Q1', '2004Q4', freq='Q')\n",
    "dfq = pd.DataFrame({'X': np.linspace(10, 25, len(qidx))}, index=qidx)\n",
    "\n",
    "mq = model(\"Y = X/X('2002Q1')*100\", modelname='fixq')\n",
    "mq(dfq, '2002Q2', '2004Q4').loc['2002Q1':'2003Q2']"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d94bbd6d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## An endogenous variable at a fixed period inside the solve span\n",
    "\n",
    "So far the fixed periods were data: `X` is exogenous, or the period lies before the periods\n",
    "solved. It is different when the variable is **endogenous** and the period is **inside** the\n",
    "solve span. In\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "> y = 0.5*y(-1) + x\n",
    "> z = y/y(2006)*100\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "solved from 2003 to 2010, `z` in 2003 needs `y` in 2006 -- a value which is only solved three\n",
    "periods later.\n",
    "\n",
    "A solver which solves **one period at a time** (`xgenr_ng`, `sim_ng`, `newton_ng`,\n",
    "`newton_fbmin_ng`) can not do that: in the periods before 2006 it would read the starting value\n",
    "of `y` in 2006. These solvers stop with an exception.\n",
    "\n",
    "The **stacked** solvers, `newtonstack_ng` and `newtonstack_fbmin_ng`, solve **all periods at\n",
    "once**. For them `y(2006)` is just one more unknown -- a column of the stacked Jacobian -- and the\n",
    "model is solved exactly. Calling the model picks a one-period solver, so the stacked solver must be\n",
    "asked for with `solver=`:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b3f7d61b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "dfi = pd.DataFrame({'X': np.linspace(1, 3, len(years)), 'Y': 1.0, 'Z': 0.0}, index=years)\n",
    "mins = model(\"\"\"\n",
    "Y = 0.5*Y(-1) + X\n",
    "Z = Y/Y(2006)*100\n",
    "\"\"\", modelname='fixinspan')\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    mins(dfi, 2003, 2010)\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f'{type(e).__name__}: {e}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e7565dc8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "res_inspan = mins(dfi, 2003, 2010, solver='newtonstack_ng')\n",
    "res_inspan.loc[2003:2010, ['X', 'Y', 'Z']]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "169d6923",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`Z` is 100 in 2006, as it must be, and in the other periods it is `Y` relative to the **solved**\n",
    "value of `Y` in 2006.\n",
    "\n",
    "The same holds when the fixed period feeds back into the simultaneous part of a model. Here\n",
    "consumption depends on income in 2006, which itself depends on consumption -- both stacked solvers\n",
    "find the same solution:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "501c2ce9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "msim = model(\"\"\"\n",
    "C = 0.6*Y + 0.2*C(-1) + 0.1*Y(2006)\n",
    "Y = C + G\n",
    "Z = Y/Y(2006)*100\n",
    "\"\"\", modelname='fixinspan_sim')\n",
    "dfs = pd.DataFrame({'G': np.linspace(20, 30, len(years)), 'C': 60.0, 'Y': 100.0, 'Z': 0.0},\n",
    "                   index=years)\n",
    "\n",
    "stack = msim.newtonstack_ng(dfs, 2003, 2010)\n",
    "fbmin = msim.newtonstack_fbmin_ng(dfs, 2003, 2010)\n",
    "print('largest difference between the two:',\n",
    "      (stack - fbmin).loc[2003:2010, ['C', 'Y', 'Z']].abs().max().max())\n",
    "stack.loc[2003:2010, ['G', 'C', 'Y', 'Z']]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "30f30c3a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Which solvers accept what:\n",
    "\n",
    "| | Exogenous `X(P)`, or `P` outside the solve span | Endogenous `X(P)`, `P` inside the solve span |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `xgenr_ng`, `sim_ng`, `newton_ng`, `newton_fbmin_ng` | yes | no -- an exception |\n",
    "| `newtonstack_ng`, `newtonstack_fbmin_ng` | yes | yes, exact |\n",
    "| `res_ng` (evaluates the equations, does not solve) | yes | yes -- reads the input values |\n",
    "| legacy solvers (`sim`, `newton`, ...) and `sim1d_ng` | no | no |\n",
    "\n",
    "A span which starts **after** the period is always fine: then `Y(2006)` is data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9b5d0df2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Rules, and what is caught when a model is made\n",
    "\n",
    "* A fixed period can not be on the left hand side: `Y(2002) = X` makes no sense as an equation.\n",
    "* No blanks inside the parentheses: `X( 2002 )` and `X( -1 )` are rejected.\n",
    "* An unsigned number of 1 to 3 digits, `X(1)`, is not allowed in a model. It is the EViews way to\n",
    "  write a lead; when equations are normalized (`fixleads`), such leads get their sign, `X(+1)`.\n",
    "  From 4 digits on, an unsigned number is a year.\n",
    "* A sub-annual period must be in quotes: `X(2002Q1)` is an error, `X('2002Q1')` is right.\n",
    "\n",
    "All of these are caught when the model is made, not when it is solved:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "27a26f7a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for text in ['Y(2002) = X', 'Y = X/X( 2002 )*100', 'Y = X(1) + Z', 'Y = X/X(2002Q1)']:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        model(text)\n",
    "        print(f'{text:22} accepted')\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        print(f'{text:22} -> {str(e).splitlines()[0]}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "29995ea2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## In estimation\n",
    "\n",
    "The estimators read an equation with Python's own parser. `X(2005)` and `X('2005Q1')` are legal\n",
    "Python -- a call of `X`, just like the lag `X(-1)` -- so nothing special is needed: the estimator\n",
    "takes the 2005 value from the data and the regressor `X/X(2005)` is the series divided by that\n",
    "value.\n",
    "\n",
    "Some synthetic data where the answer is known: `Y` depends on `X` relative to its 2005 value."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "eab2cc7b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rng = np.random.default_rng(1)\n",
    "eyears = list(range(2000, 2021))\n",
    "n = len(eyears)\n",
    "dfe = pd.DataFrame({'X': np.linspace(10, 30, n) + rng.normal(0, 1, n),\n",
    "                    'Z': rng.normal(0, 1, n)}, index=eyears)\n",
    "dfe['Y'] = 2.0 + 3.0 * dfe.X / dfe.loc[2005, 'X'] + 0.5 * dfe.Z + rng.normal(0, 0.05, n)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c440e6be",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Estimated with the fixed period, and with the old workaround -- a column holding the 2005 value\n",
    "in every row. The estimates are the same, and close to the 2, 3 and 0.5 the data was made from:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "81e9f739",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ols = Estimate_ols(org_eq='Y = C(1) + C(2)*(X/X(2005)) + C(3)*Z',\n",
    "                   input_df=dfe, smpl=(2001, 2020), ecm=False)\n",
    "workaround = Estimate_ols(org_eq='Y = C(1) + C(2)*(X/X_AT_2005) + C(3)*Z',\n",
    "                          input_df=dfe.assign(X_AT_2005=dfe.loc[2005, 'X']),\n",
    "                          smpl=(2001, 2020), ecm=False)\n",
    "pd.DataFrame({'X(2005)': ols.coef_estimate_dict, 'workaround': workaround.coef_estimate_dict})"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "32fff477",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The non-linear estimator works the same way. It defaults to an error correction equation\n",
    "(`ecm=True`), which this is not:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6aa5e5c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "nls = Estimate_nls_lmfit(org_eq='Y = C(1) + C(2)*(X/X(2005)) + C(3)*Z',\n",
    "                         input_df=dfe, smpl=(2001, 2020), ecm=False)\n",
    "pd.Series(nls.coef_estimate_dict)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c15e2625",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### While building a model\n",
    "\n",
    "In `Makemodel` (and in `%%Makemymodel`) an equation tagged `<est=...>` is estimated while the\n",
    "model is built, and `X(2005)` stays a fixed period through estimation and normalization. Here the\n",
    "estimated equation for `y` is followed by an identity which indexes `y` to 2005:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a8f60b80",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "Mfix = Makemodel(\"\"\"\n",
    "## Y relative to the level of X in 2005\n",
    "><est=ols,smpl=2001 2020> y = c(1) + c(2)*(x/x(2005)) + c(3)*z\n",
    "\n",
    "## Y indexed to 2005\n",
    "> w = y/y(2005)*100\n",
    "\"\"\", input_df=dfe)\n",
    "Mfix.show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "598bbeec",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`w` reads the **endogenous** `y` in 2005. Solved over the whole estimation sample, 2005 is inside\n",
    "the solve span, so this needs a stacked solver; solved from 2006 on, `y(2005)` is data and any\n",
    "solver will do:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "65cc38a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "mfixest = Mfix.mmodel\n",
    "whole = mfixest(dfe, 2001, 2020, solver='newtonstack_ng')\n",
    "print('w in 2005:', whole.loc[2005, 'W'])\n",
    "whole.loc[2003:2008, ['X', 'Z', 'Y', 'W']]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "17826645",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Quick reference\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "> index = x/x(2015)*100           # a year: unsigned, at least 4 digits\n",
    "> index = x/x('2015Q1')*100       # a quarter or a month: the index label in quotes\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "* Only the ng solvers evaluate a fixed period; calling the model picks one.\n",
    "* An endogenous variable at a fixed period **inside** the solve span needs a stacked solver:\n",
    "  `mymodel(df, start, end, solver='newtonstack_ng')` (or `newtonstack_fbmin_ng`).\n",
    "* The period must be a row of the DataFrame.\n",
    "* The estimators and `Makemodel` keep `X(2005)` a fixed period; the estimates equal those of the\n",
    "  workaround with an exogenous column holding the 2005 value."
   ]
  }
 ],
